        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00250:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Ethyl isopropyl ether reacts with hydrogen iodide, forming intermediate in which ethyl carbon is labeled less hindered, is attacked by iodide (S N 2) to produce isopropyl alcohol and iodoethane."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_18_03_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
